{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2177-08-03 15:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee, one of the hospitalists. You were admitted for right upper quadrant pain and nausea. Can you tell me more about your symptoms?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2177-08-03 15:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I’ve had this pain before—same spot, under my ribs. It started a few days ago. I had a low-grade fever at home, around 99.6, and felt nauseous. My hepatologist started me on doxycycline, but I wasn’t getting better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2177-08-03 15:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Given your history of primary sclerosing cholangitis and past cholangitis episodes, this could be another flare. We’ll run some tests to confirm."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2177-08-03 15:28:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I was worried it might be. I’ve had this so many times. Is it serious?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2177-08-03 15:29:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s treatable. We’ll start antibiotics right away to cover any infection, even though you’re not running a high fever now. We also need to check if there’s a stone blocking your bile ducts."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2177-08-03 15:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember last time there was a stone. Can’t they just remove it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2177-08-03 15:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll find out. You’re scheduled for an ultrasound first. If we see a stone, we may need an MRCP or ERCP to get a better look and possibly remove it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2177-08-03 16:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your ultrasound is back. It shows a retained stone in the central intrahepatic ducts, possibly in the right hepatic duct. No bile duct dilation, which is good, but it could still be causing your symptoms."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2177-08-03 16:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s the same stone again? Why can’t they get it out?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2177-08-03 16:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s in a tricky spot. But we’re not giving up. We’re ordering an MRCP tomorrow for a more detailed view. That’ll help us plan the next step."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2177-08-03 16:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And the antibiotics? You said you’d start me on something."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2177-08-03 16:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’re starting IV meropenem. It’s broad-spectrum and safe for you, given your allergies to sulfa and penicillin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2177-08-03 16:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. I had diarrhea last time on doxycycline."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2177-08-03 16:26:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll monitor that. For now, focus on resting. We’ll check your labs and see how you respond."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2177-08-04 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your blood and urine cultures came back negative—no infection in the blood. That’s reassuring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2177-08-04 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I don’t have an infection?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2177-08-04 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The cultures are negative, but your symptoms and history suggest cholangitis. We’re continuing meropenem because it’s likely a bile duct issue that doesn’t always show up in blood tests."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2177-08-04 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Makes sense. What about the MRCP?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2177-08-04 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s scheduled for tomorrow morning. It’ll show us the exact location of the stone and the condition of your bile ducts."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2177-08-05 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your MRCP is done. It shows a 5 mm filling defect in the common hepatic duct—likely a stone. There’s also confirmation of your PSC changes: fibrosis and irregular ducts."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2177-08-05 10:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So they can remove it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2177-08-05 10:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. We’ve scheduled an ERCP for tomorrow. We’ll try to remove the stone using a balloon sweep. Given it’s embedded, we may use a special scope—Spyglass—to see it directly and take biopsies."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2177-08-05 10:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Biopsies? Is there a cancer concern?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2177-08-05 10:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s precautionary. Sometimes tissue grows over stones, and we want to make sure it’s not abnormal. But your prior tests were negative, so we’re optimistic."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2177-08-05 10:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I trust you. When will I know how it went?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2177-08-05 10:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The procedure is at 12 tomorrow. I’ll come by afterward to update you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2177-08-06 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, you’re back from the ERCP. The good news: we found an embedded stone in the common hepatic duct. We used Spyglass and biopsies to loosen it, then cleared a portion with a balloon sweep."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2177-08-06 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s gone?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2177-08-06 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "At least part of it. We got a piece out, and the duct is now draining better. The tissue over the stone showed chronic inflammation, which fits your PSC. The biopsies will be checked for IgG4 to rule out another condition, but that’s routine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2177-08-06 14:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the antibiotics?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2177-08-06 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re still improving. We’re switching from IV meropenem to oral ciprofloxacin. You’ll take it for 9 more days at home. After that, resume your rifaximin for prevention."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2177-08-06 14:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I can go home soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2177-08-06 14:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Likely by Friday. We’ll watch your labs and make sure you’re stable. Your liver enzymes are already improving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2177-08-07 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Morning. Your labs are trending well. WBC is normal, bilirubin is down. We’re confident you’re on the mend."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2177-08-07 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. I feel better already. Less pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2177-08-07 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. We’ll keep you on cipro, ursodiol, and your other meds. We’re adding a mild laxative, senna, in case the oxycodone for pain causes constipation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2177-08-07 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had that before. I’ll drink more water."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2177-08-07 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Fiber too—fruits and veggies. You’ll follow up with Dr. ___ at the liver center in two weeks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2177-08-08 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All set for discharge tomorrow. Your final labs look good. No fever, pain is minimal, and you’re eating well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2177-08-08 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m relieved. Will I keep getting these stones?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2177-08-08 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "With PSC, there’s a risk, but rifaximin helps reduce flares. We’ll monitor with imaging as needed. The ERCP helped clear the blockage, which should reduce recurrence for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2177-08-08 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my other conditions—thyroid, blood pressure?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2177-08-08 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All stable. You’ll continue levothyroxine, lisinopril, furosemide, and omeprazole. No changes needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2177-08-08 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And depression? I’ve been feeling down with all these hospital visits."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2177-08-08 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I’m sorry you’re feeling that way. Keep taking your escitalopram. Please mention this at your follow-up—mental health is part of your care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2177-08-08 10:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you for listening."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2177-08-09 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’re cleared to go home. Take ciprofloxacin twice daily for 9 days, then restart rifaximin. Use oxycodone only if needed for pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2177-08-09 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And the senna?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2177-08-09 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Only if you’re constipated. Drink fluids and eat fiber first. Call if you have fever, worsening pain, or can’t keep food down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2177-08-09 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you, Dr. Lee. Happy Birthday, by the way—I saw it on your badge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2177-08-09 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Oh—thank you! That’s very kind. Take care, and I hope your next visit is just a routine check-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2177-08-09 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Me too. I’ll see you or Dr. ___ soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2177-08-09 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, she’ll get your ERCP biopsy results and follow up. You’re doing well—keep it up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2177-08-09 08:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2177-08-09 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. The team will help you with discharge paperwork and getting home safely."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2177-08-03 15:20:00",
    "admission_end": "2177-08-09 12:50:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with a history of primary sclerosing cholangitis and cirrhosis was admitted for recurrent right upper quadrant pain and nausea, consistent with cholangitis. She had been started on doxycycline by her hepatologist without improvement. Initial labs showed mild abnormalities, and blood and urine cultures were negative. Imaging revealed a 5 mm obstructive stone in the common hepatic duct. She underwent ERCP with Spyglass cholangioscopy, during which an embedded stone was identified and partially removed using biopsies and balloon sweeps. She was treated with IV meropenem, transitioned to oral ciprofloxacin for completion at home, and showed clinical improvement. Her chronic conditions, including hypertension, hypothyroidism, GERD, and depression, were managed throughout. She was discharged home with a plan to complete antibiotics, resume rifaximin, and follow up with the liver center.",
    "problems": [
      "Calculus of bile duct without mention of cholecystitis, with obstruction",
      "Esophageal varices in diseases classified elsewhere, without mention of bleeding",
      "Cirrhosis of liver without mention of alcohol",
      "Body Mass Index 30.0-30.9, adult",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Obesity, unspecified",
      "Unspecified acquired hypothyroidism",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified"
    ]
  }
}
